Lots of us have tried porting the MIT X release to OSF/1. This is using the
same source code that works on Ultrix. We've probably all found that even though
the sources compile fairly easily, the executables don't work.

I asked somebody inside DEC who Knows The Truth about this. He's an exact
quote (with permission) of what he said:

"The rumor about unmodified X11R5 not working on Alpha OSF/1 is true.  We
had to fix the source not just for coding practices (you can't keep a
64-bit pointer in a 32-bit integer) but also substantively for the
libraries, because X is a 32-bit protocol and there had to be some way to
pass 64-bit entities."

He goes on to say:

"We've offered the changes to the Consortium, and MIT has decided to
incorporate them into X11R6 but not into X11R5 -- their decision.
