The 300 may have run a field test version, because there was a separate
version for the 300 (1.2A) in order to support the new CPU (i.e. V1.2,
the release version would not support it).

A generic thing to look out for even with the release versions is that
the unified buffer cache is shipped with ubcmaxpercent == 100, i.e.
file intensive operations may eat all of your memory. I usually recommend
running with a much lower setting for ubcmaxpercent (50 at most).

